 you aren't paying a premium for upside strikes.\n- **Drift:** The yearly series is 24% in 2024, 26% in 2025 and 27% in 2026. That series has only three points, so I can't say more about where 27% sits in its range.\n- **Term structure:** Implied volatility is 26% for Jan-2027, 27% for Jan-2028 and 27.5% for Jan-2029. It is nearly flat, so going further out costs only about 1.5 volatility points. The longer expiries aren't costly on volatility alone.\n\nI didn't have premiums, strikes, delta or an underlying price, so I couldn't check price against a fair-value estimate. My conclusion rests on implied volatility alone.\n\nWhether adding is attractive therefore depends on your view of the underlying business, not on cheap options. Other nodes are covering that. The related findings so far are mixed:\n- Pellham Power plans 2027 capital spending up 18%, with a transformer tender of about C$900M due to award in Q1 2027.\n- Data-centre grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027, slower than in 2026.\n- Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp.\n\nIf you add, the Jan-2028 expiry looks like a reasonable balance, since it costs only about 1 volatility point more than Jan-2027.\n\nSources: `vltx-leaps` snapshot, and the `vltx_iv_history` and `vltx_iv_term` series.","ttft_ms":2375,"type":"result","duration_ms":43279,"uuid":"c3d1c2c8-fae6-424e-b37b-436dbbf21e49","ttft_stream_ms":1475,"time_to_request_ms":350,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":20,"system_prompt":39,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":11,"input_attachments":92,"input_hooks":18,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":19,"tool_pool_refresh":6,"init_message":26,"init_frame_send":12,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":11,"message_prep":10,"model_config_wait":9,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":23,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":11,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":13,"request_build":24},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_reque